From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 19:30:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(dsv41): serve GLP at WEIGHTLESS_STEER_ALPHA and log
 canonical boot identity

Support serve-time GLP dose override via WEIGHTLESS_STEER_ALPHA (replacing
glp.alpha_default without editing the pinned GGUF file, fail-closed on
non-positive/non-finite/non-numeric values, and included in
envs.compile_factors()) and emit one canonical GLP boot identity line
carrying file_sha256, content_sha256, spec_version, hook, layers,
alpha_default, and effective alpha (source=file|override).

Also validate WEIGHTLESS_STEER_ALPHA in glp.py CLI main() so pre-boot
doctor reader checks catch bad doses before container start.

Upstream-base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354
Rationale: Keeps GLP alpha a serve-time parameter per the GLP spec so doses can be recalibrated without breaking GGUF sha256 pinning, and makes booted vector identity and effective dose unambiguous in logs.
Quality: Unset WEIGHTLESS_STEER_ALPHA preserves exact file glp.alpha_default behavior; fold and attention-write paths share the single GLPSteering.alpha tensor buffer.
Tests: pytest tests/models/test_deepseek_v4_1_glp.py (61 passed on CPU container without libcuda; 2 GPU-kernel import tests skipped/requiring CUDA).
Upstream-status: Local DeepSeek-V4.1 GLP serve-time alpha override and boot identity logging.
